# Confluence Update (Vecima Atlassian)

**Wiki:** `https://vecima.atlassian.net/wiki` · **MCP:** `user-atlassian` (`confluence_get_page`, `confluence_update_page`)

## Workflow (mandatory)

1. **`confluence_get_page`** — record `version`, check for `{toc}` / `macro-diagram` / existing `code` macros.
2. **Draft in chat** — section title, bullet summary of changes (not full page dump). **Wait for user confirmation** unless they explicitly said “更新到 Confluence” / “publish now”.
3. **Update** — prefer **partial `body.storage` insert/replace** at a section anchor; bump `version` + `version_comment`.
4. **Report** — page URL, new version number, what changed.

**Never** full-page markdown replace via MCP if the page has `{toc}` or other Confluence-native macros — it strips them.

## Content style

- **Technical & concise** — logic and call flow over prose; tables for comparisons/counters.
- **No line-level code dumps** unless user asks — file/function names OK, skip `file.c:862-874` unless debugging.
- **English or 中文** — match the page’s existing language.
- One **Conclusion** line per major section, then diagrams/flows, then short Verify/Mitigation if relevant.

## Diagrams (required when explaining architecture or RX/TX paths)

Include **both** where applicable:

| Type | Use for |
|------|---------|
| **System block** | Components, pools, cross-process fan-out |
| **Flow / decision** | Branches, drop points, counters (`msg_too_many_auto`, etc.) |

### Preferred: ASCII in `{code}` macro (reliable on Vecima)

Match existing pages on `~Oreo.Yang` space:

- `ac:name="code"`, `language=none`, `breakoutMode=wide`, `breakoutWidth=760`
- Monospace box-drawing (`│`, `├─`, `└─`, `+---+`) or simple arrows
- Label: `h4` above each block (e.g. “System view”, “RX allocation flow”)

### Avoid: `macro-diagram` (Mermaid)

Shows **“Error loading the extension!”** on this instance (pre-existing). Do not add new `macro-diagram` unless user confirms the app is fixed.

### Fallback

- Confluence **table** for simple pipelines
- PNG/SVG from [mermaid.live](https://mermaid.live) only if user wants pretty figures and accepts manual upkeep

## Preserve on edit

- `{toc}` macro at page top
- Existing `code` / diagram style consistency
- Section numbering (`§4.6`, `5) …`) unless restructuring is requested

## Vecima XPON doc patterns (reference)

- Per-process isolation: netconf vs `example_user_appl` — separate `transport stat` / CLD
- Transport pools: `free_auto_list` (AUTO/indications) vs `free_req_list` (sync API)
- Drop before unpack → no CLD, no journal (`msg_too_many_auto`)

## Do not

- Publish without confirmation on exploratory drafts
- Use one-off Python/REST scripts when MCP partial update suffices
- Commit Confluence content to git unless user asks
